From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:45:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom: wcnss: allow MSM8226 shared MX votes

SM-T531's captured stock DT connects both CPU CPR VDD_MX and Pronto
VDDMX to PM8226 L3, whose maximum is 1337500 uV. Its turbo CPU corner
requires 1280000 uV on this rail. Pronto v1's fixed 1150000 uV upper
vote conflicts with that requirement; regulator_check_consumers reports
an invalid 1280000-1150000 interval, and the WCNSS driver ignores it.

Allow the stock shared-rail maximum only for MSM8226 Pronto v1, while
preserving the 950000 uV minimum. Other variants and supplies retain
their existing ranges. Propagate voltage-vote failures so firmware cannot
start after an unsatisfied supply request.

Reference: captured SM-T531 qcom,pronto-vddmx-supply and regulator-3-ao;
LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226
3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256,
arch/arm/boot/dts/msm8226-regulator.dtsi and cpr-regulator.c.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_wcnss.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_wcnss.c
index 55672c009..37aa6c073 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_wcnss.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_wcnss.c
@@ -478,10 +478,21 @@ static int wcnss_init_regulators(struct qcom_wcnss *wcnss,
 		return ret;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < num_vregs; i++) {
-		if (info[i].max_voltage)
-			regulator_set_voltage(bulk[i].consumer,
-					      info[i].min_voltage,
-					      info[i].max_voltage);
+		if (info[i].max_voltage) {
+			int max_voltage = info[i].max_voltage;
+
+			/* MSM8226 shares MX with the CPU corner-ceiling vote. */
+			if (data == &pronto_v1_data &&
+			    of_machine_is_compatible("qcom,msm8226") &&
+			    !strcmp(info[i].name, "vddmx"))
+				max_voltage = 1337500;
+
+			ret = regulator_set_voltage(bulk[i].consumer,
+						    info[i].min_voltage, max_voltage);
+			if (ret)
+				return dev_err_probe(wcnss->dev, ret,
+						     "Failed to vote %s voltage\n", info[i].name);
+		}
 
 		if (info[i].load_uA)
 			regulator_set_load(bulk[i].consumer, info[i].load_uA);
